摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Generate Function, MCP, Agent Skill, and offline test packages from existing code; installable as a DeepSeek Harness bundle.","id":"gh:1304163962","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"Code2Skill","slug":"leechen298/Code2Skill","topics":["agent-skills","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Generate Function, MCP, Agent Skill, and offline test packages from existing code; installable as a "},{"id":"p1s2","text":"DeepSeek Harness bundle."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Code2Skill"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Code2Skill is a collection of installable Agent Skills that helps coding agents understand business "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"functionality in user-authorized frontend, backend, or full-stack source code, then generate Functio"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ns, MCP tools, workflow Skills, and offline tests for other agents to use."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"This repository is distinct from ant-intl/Code2Skill, a research implementation for synthesizing sou"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"rce-grounded procedural skill records and retrieval indexes from code; the two projects serve differ"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"procedural skill records and retrieval indexes from code; the two projects serve different purposes."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Current release: v1.2.0."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Functions and MCP tools provide business capabilities. Skills guide an agent in using those capabili"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ties. The consuming agent still decides whether to call a tool, what to clarify, how to interpret a "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"response, and what to do next."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"## What It Does"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"- Generates capabilities from business invocation points that actually exist in source code. Client-"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"backed features start from calls made by the client or consumer; projects without a client start fro"},{"id":"p10s3","text":"m user-specified public APIs, RPCs, services, messages, or task entry points and follow their public"},{"id":"p10s4","text":" request, response, and contract types as needed.\n- Identifies independently completable goals withi"},{"id":"p10s5","text":"n a user-specified page, directory, feature, or public entry point.\n- Places field provenance, selec"},{"id":"p10s6","text":"ted-record handoffs between tools, request assembly, and deterministic transformations in Functions."},{"id":"p10s7","text":"\n- Generates a Skill for each primary goal while reusing the necessary Functions and MCP tools.\n- De"},{"id":"p10s8","text":"faults to offline technical validation and does not call live business APIs."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Supported Agents"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"You can run Code2Skill with mainstream coding agents such as Codex, Claude Code, and Kimi Code. Gene"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"rated Skills can be installed in Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, OpenClaw, and other environments that s"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"upport Agent Skills."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"See the `skills` CLI compatibility list for more environments. To perform live business operations, "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"register the generated MCP server as described in each package's `MCP-SETUP.md`."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Install all three Skills with the standard Agent Skills CLI:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- `code2skill-generate`: generates Functions, MCP tools, workflow Skills, and offline tests.\n- `code"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"2skill-review-flow`: checks whether a user can complete the main goals through the generated workflo"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ws.\n- `code2skill-review-source`: reviews request fields, transformations, and invocation chains aga"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"inst the authorized source code."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Routine generation only requires `code2skill-generate`. Run the two review Skills independently when"},{"id":"p18s2","text":" needed. The three Skill instructions and default generated-document templates are available in Engl"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ish and Chinese; user-facing output follows the language of the request. The optional legacy `strict"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"-export-v1` compatibility mode still emits `zh-CN` documentation. See the installation guide for mig"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"ration from older versions, generated-package dependencies, and MCP registration."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"### DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness users can install the three Skills as a Bundle in a selected profile:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"See the DeepSeek Harness integration guide for installation, verification, headless profiles, and re"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"moval. Generated business MCP servers must still be registered separately according to their own `MC"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"usiness MCP servers must still be registered separately according to their own `MCP-SETUP.md` files."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Usage Boundaries"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Code2Skill produces runnable, editable first drafts of business capabilities. It does not prove that"},{"id":"p24s2","text":" every business rule or real environment has been validated. Results depend on the generation model,"},{"id":"p24s3","text":" source completeness, and the scope the user authorizes."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"For complex writes or high-value workflows, review cross-tool data provenance, same-name field seman"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"tics, deterministic request transformations, goal-specific prerequisites, attachment uploads, and do"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"wnstream bindings. Use `code2skill-review-flow` to check the main workflow and `code2skill-review-so"},{"id":"p25s4","text":"urce` to inspect critical source semantics. Offline tests do not replace real API or deployment acce"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"o inspect critical source semantics. Offline tests do not replace real API or deployment acceptance."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Quick Start"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Invoke the generation Skill inside the target repository and explicitly authorize the source roots i"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"eration Skill inside the target repository and explicitly authorize the source roots it may inspect:"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"For independent reviews:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Generated Package"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The logical output stays consistent while file extensions, dependencies, and startup commands follow"},{"id":"p32s2","text":" the target stack's runtime profile. The current `core-export-v1` default is implemented by the `nod"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"'s runtime profile. The current `core-export-v1` default is implemented by the `node-stdio` profile:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Each generated `MCP-SETUP.md` records the runtime language, dependency installation, startup command"},{"id":"p34s2","text":", environment variables, unmet prerequisites, and MCP registration steps. A Skill being installed, a"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"n MCP server being connected, and the live business workflow being validated are three separate stat"},{"id":"p34s4","text":"CP server being connected, and the live business workflow being validated are three separate states."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Generation Results"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"Three runs against the same anonymized, multi-goal source package:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"| Generation model / configuration | Date | Generation time | Composite reference score |\n|---|---|-"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"--:|---:|\n| GPT-5.6 Sol (Ultra) | 2026-07-24 | 47m 45s | **9.4** |\n| Kimi K3 (Max reasoning) | 2026-"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"07-24 | about 93m | **8.9** |\n| GPT-5.6 Sol (High) | 2026-07-24 | 20m 29s | **8.4** |"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Timing ends when generation and that run's offline validation finish; it excludes later scoring, dir"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"ectory cleanup, installation, and deployment. See the evaluation report for the two scoring systems,"},{"id":"p38s3","text":" methodology, and privacy boundaries."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"## Documentation"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"- Install Skills, generated dependencies, and MCP servers\n- Generated package structure and design p"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"rinciples\n- Runtime-neutral generation design\n- Workflow-aware generation design\n- Optional advanced"},{"id":"p40s3","text":" validation\n- Models, scoring, and anonymized evaluation results\n- Full documentation index"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
